{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "central_D_lat_zero_grad_bc",
    "description": "Centered first derivative along latitude with zero-gradient boundary rows on the latlon grid. Matches D(f, wrt: lat), a PER-DEGREE derivative (see grids/latlon/grid.esm for the physical-units metric recipe). Interior rows [2, NLAT-1]: the imported centered-difference stencil. Boundary rows j=1 and j=NLAT: one-sided differences (f[i,2] - f[i,1]) / dlat_deg and (f[i,NLAT] - f[i,NLAT-1]) / dlat_deg encoding the zero-gradient condition; the three regions tile the axes, so the discretized derivative is fully defined with its BC (esm-spec 9.6.8). On the GLOBAL recipe (lat0_deg = -90, dlat_deg = 180/(NLAT-1)) the boundary rows are the poles themselves, and zero-gradient there is a deliberately CRUDE pole treatment — standard for exemplar transport, adequate for fields whose meridional gradient vanishes at the poles (any regular scalar field on the sphere has d f/d lat = 0 at the poles along every meridian), but it neither couples the pole rows across longitude nor conserves anything through the pole; proper pole handling (averaged polar caps, or an unstructured cap) is a different rule/grid. On a REGIONAL grid the same rule is an ordinary zero-gradient (homogeneous Neumann) frame boundary. The face values are FULL-RANK aggregates (singleton output range on the lat axis) so every binding's simulator fills the (NLON x 1) regions without rank promotion — the rank-reduced face form of the esm-spec 9.6.8 worked example only fills leading-axis faces portably. `dlat_deg` is a free name resolving to the consuming model's meridional spacing variable (consumer-supplied geometry contract). The one-sided faces are O(dlat_deg) locally, which preserves global 2nd-order convergence for boundary-compatible solutions (see the MMS problem problems/latlon_advection_meridional_zero_grad.esm). Match scoping: the pattern is `wrt: lat` plus the constraint `where: {f: {shape: [lon, lat]}}` (esm-spec 9.6.1), so it fires only on the meridional derivative of a bare field declared over this grid's lon x lat index sets — not on any unrelated D(., wrt: lat) reusing the axis name, and, under import-edge renaming (esm-spec 9.7.7), the wrt literal and the where shape follow the renamed axis together, so two latlon instances coexist scoped to their own meshes. The constraint requires a bare shaped variable; a consumer differentiating a compound inline expression must bind it to a declared lon x lat observed first.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:rule", "family:finite_difference", "grid:latlon", "op:D", "axes:lon,lat", "order:2", "stencil_width:3", "bc:zero_gradient", "spec:9.6.8"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.12 (one-sided boundary treatment)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Williamson, D. L., Drake, J. B., Hack, J. J., Jakob, R., & Swarztrauber, P. N. (1992). A standard test set for numerical approximations to the shallow water equations in spherical geometry. Journal of Computational Physics, 102(1), 211-224. (Context for pole treatments on latitude-longitude grids.)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    { "ref": "../stencils/central_D_lat_interior.esm" }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "central_D_lat_zero_grad_bc": {
      "params": ["f"],
      "match": { "op": "D", "args": ["f"], "wrt": "lat" },
      "where": { "f": { "shape": ["lon", "lat"] } },
      "body": {
        "op": "makearray",
        "args": [],
        "regions": [
          [[1, "NLON"], [2, { "op": "-", "args": ["NLAT", 1] }]],
          [[1, "NLON"], [1, 1]],
          [[1, "NLON"], ["NLAT", "NLAT"]]
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "central_D_lat_interior",
            "bindings": { "f": "f" }
          },
          {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
            "args": ["f"],
            "ranges": { "i": { "from": "lon" }, "j": [1, 1] },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", "i", 2] },
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", "i", 1] }
                  ]
                },
                "dlat_deg"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
            "args": ["f"],
            "ranges": { "i": { "from": "lon" }, "j": ["NLAT", "NLAT"] },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", "i", "NLAT"] },
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", "i", { "op": "-", "args": ["NLAT", 1] }] }
                  ]
                },
                "dlat_deg"
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
